<Legal
  title="Privacy"
  description="What Bubo stores about you, where it lives, and who else sees it. Downloading the app needs no account at all."
  path="/privacy"
  updated="30 July 2026"
>
  <h1>Privacy</h1>
  <p class="lede">
    Bubo itself runs on your Mac and does not need an account. An account exists
    for one reason: to hold a Pro key and the Macs it is running on.
  </p>

  <h2>If you only download Bubo</h2>
  <p>
    Nothing. The downloads are open to anyone, signed in or not, and the app
    does not ask you to register.
  </p>

  <h2>If you make an account</h2>
  <p>
    Accounts are handled by Clerk, which stores your email address and whatever
    name you give it. Passwords never reach us; Clerk holds them.
  </p>
  <p>
    Against that account we store your plan, your license key, and the Macs the
    key has been activated on. That is the whole record.
  </p>

  <h2>If you buy Pro</h2>
  <p>
    Payment is taken by Paddle, who are the merchant of record. Card details go
    to Paddle and never touch our servers; we never see them. Paddle tells us
    that a payment completed and which account it belongs to, and we issue the
    key from that.
  </p>

  <h2>Who else gets your data</h2>
  <p>
    Clerk, for accounts. Paddle, for payments. Vercel, which hosts these sites
    and keeps ordinary server logs, and Vercel Analytics, which counts page
    views on this site without cookies or cross-site tracking. Nobody else, and
    none of it is sold or used for advertising.
  </p>

  <h2>Deleting it</h2>
  <p>
    Email <a href="mailto:support@weekndlabs.com">support@weekndlabs.com</a> and
    we will delete your account and everything stored against it. If you want a
    copy of that record first, ask and we will send it.
  </p>
</Legal>
